From 859c037e10c54da2a48e9c3891f243fe25c06e47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:31:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 68/97] script: video textures, puppet animation layers,
 particle systems, the other events

The rest of SceneScript's documented interfaces (lib.sceneScript.d.ts 2.8), against what the
library's scripts call:
- IImageLayer.getVideoTexture / IVideoTexture (3243449890, 3326873240): play, pause, stop (to the
  start), isPlaying, get/setCurrentTime (a seek waits until mpv has the video), duration, rate, loop,
  addEndedCallback (mpv keeps the last frame of a video that doesn't loop). undefined for a layer
  whose texture isn't a video.
- IAnimationLayer on puppet layers (3363252053, 3414858021's sway layers, 3326873240):
  getAnimationLayerCount, getAnimationLayer (name or index, one object per layer), fps, frameCount,
  duration, name, rate, blend, visible, play / pause / stop, isPlaying, get/setFrame,
  addEndedCallback (each loop wrap, mirror turn, single finish), createAnimationLayer,
  playSingleAnimation (plays once, then removed), destroyAnimationLayer. Scripts on an animation
  layer's rate / visible / blend run, with thisObject that IAnimationLayer.
- Bones: getBoneCount, getBoneIndex, getBoneParentIndex, get/setBoneTransform (world),
  get/setLocalBoneTransform / Angles / Origin (a script's local pose over the animations'). Bone
  physics and blend shapes are no-ops (LWE has neither; no library scene uses them).
- IParticleSystem: play, pause (no new particles), stop (all gone), isPlaying, emitParticles,
  instance (IParticleSystemInstance: the instanceoverride values, live, controlpoint0..7 too).
- IEffect.setMaterialProperty (the effect's shader constant of that name, live), getMaterial.
- Events: applyGeneralSettings ({ language } from the locale, once on load), animationEvent
  ({ name, frame }, value) as a keyframe timeline passes its `options.events` (also those passed
  before the script started), destroy () before the scene goes and for a destroyed layer.
- The scene's clear colour is set every frame: a video texture's player (mpv) left its own (black)
  behind, so every scene with a video texture cleared black; a script's IScene.clearcolor now shows.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md (SceneScript coverage); docs/player/reports/scene-health.md
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
